Third-party code in job-radar

Parts of job-radar are copied or adapted from Job Market Radar ("Radarak"),
https://github.com/moamenmoussa172/job-market-radar, under the MIT License below. Each copied part says so where it starts:

- job_radar/fx.py: the ECB rates reader and the currency pegs (from dags/jobradar/fx.py and dbt/seeds/currency_pegs.csv)
- sql/schema.sql: the skills added in 2026-10 (dbt/seeds/skills.csv) and core.geo_pattern (dbt/seeds/geo_patterns.csv)
- job_radar/steps.py: the work-permit signal patterns (dbt/models/intermediate/int_job_signals.sql)
- job_radar/tech.py: the tech-job title filter (dags/jobradar/filters.py)
- sql/schema.sql: core.role_family, core.seniority and core.role_track (dbt/models/intermediate/int_postings_classified.sql,
  dbt/seeds/role_tracks.csv)
- job_radar/sources/boards.csv: the first company boards (dags/jobradar/company_boards.csv)

